{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1374","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Zero Remainder Array"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array $$$a$$$ consisting of $$$n$$$ positive integers."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Initially, you have an integer $$$x = 0$$$. During one move, you can do one of the following two operations:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly one"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$i$$$ from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ and increase $$$a_i$$$ by $$$x$$$ ($$$a_i := a_i + x$$$), then increase $$$x$$$ by $$$1$$$ ($$$x := x + 1$$$). "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Just increase $$$x$$$ by $$$1$$$ ($$$x := x + 1$$$). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first operation can be applied "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"no more than once"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" to each $$$i$$$ from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to find the minimum number of moves required to obtain such an array that each its element is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"divisible by"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$k$$$ (the value $$$k$$$ is given)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have to answer $$$t$$$ independent test cases. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains one integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 2 \\cdot 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases. Then $$$t$$$ test cases follow."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the test case contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5; 1 \\le k \\le 10^9$$$) — the length of $$$a$$$ and the required divisior. The second line of the test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le 10^9$$$), where $$$a_i$$$ is the $$$i$$$-th element of $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$ ($$$\\sum n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print the answer — the minimum number of moves required to obtain such an array that each its element is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"divisible by"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$k$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n4 3\n1 2 1 3\n10 6\n8 7 1 8 3 7 5 10 8 9\n5 10\n20 100 50 20 100500\n10 25\n24 24 24 24 24 24 24 24 24 24\n8 8\n1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n18\n0\n227\n8\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the first test case of the example:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$x=0$$$, $$$a = [1, 2, 1, 3]$$$. Just increase $$$x$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$x=1$$$, $$$a = [1, 2, 1, 3]$$$. Add $$$x$$$ to the second element and increase $$$x$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$x=2$$$, $$$a = [1, 3, 1, 3]$$$. Add $$$x$$$ to the third element and increase $$$x$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$x=3$$$, $$$a = [1, 3, 3, 3]$$$. Add $$$x$$$ to the fourth element and increase $$$x$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$x=4$$$, $$$a = [1, 3, 3, 6]$$$. Just increase $$$x$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$x=5$$$, $$$a = [1, 3, 3, 6]$$$. Add $$$x$$$ to the first element and increase $$$x$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$x=6$$$, $$$a = [6, 3, 3, 6]$$$. We obtained the required array. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that you can't add $$$x$$$ to the same element more than once"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1374D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1374/problem/D"}